From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libril: build the Samsung libril with ril.samsung_libril

For the LTE build of the SM-T815 (WITH_LTE=true sets the soong config
variable ril.samsung_libril, together with ril.use_aosp_rild): build
the Samsung libril sources of hardware/samsung/ril/libril under this
module name, so that the Soong rild links against them and loads
Samsung's libsec-ril.so. The Samsung libril registers HIDL IRadio 1.0
("slot1"); hardware/lineage/interfaces/radio/1.4/legacy wraps it as
IRadio 1.4 for the framework.

hardware/samsung has the same sources as a make module named libril
(BOARD_PROVIDES_LIBRIL), which cannot be used next to this Soong module
of the same name, and a Soong rild cannot link against a make module.

With the variable set: the sources come from the filegroup
//hardware/samsung:libril_samsung_srcs (patches/hardware_samsung/0001),
hardware/samsung/ril/libril and hardware/samsung/ril/include (Samsung
ril.h) come first in the include path, the OEM hook HAL library is
linked, SAMSUNG_NEXT_GEN_MODEM is defined (as the make build does for
BOARD_MODEM_TYPE ss333) and warnings are not errors. Without it the
module is unchanged.
---
diff --git a/libril/Android.bp b/libril/Android.bp
index 1a8cbec..141e032 100644
--- a/libril/Android.bp
+++ b/libril/Android.bp
@@ -33,13 +33,21 @@ license {
 cc_library_shared {
     name: "libril",
     vendor: true,
-    srcs: [
-        "ril.cpp",
-        "ril_event.cpp",
-        "ril_service.cpp",
-        "RilSapSocket.cpp",
-        "sap_service.cpp",
-    ],
+    // gts210ltexx: with the soong config variable ril.samsung_libril set to true, build the
+    // Samsung libril of hardware/samsung/ril/libril (HIDL IRadio 1.0, the Samsung request and
+    // response tables, the Samsung structure layout in hardware/samsung/ril/include) under this
+    // module name, for Samsung's legacy libsec-ril.so. The make module of the same name in
+    // hardware/samsung cannot be used: rild is a Soong module, and the two "libril" would clash.
+    srcs: select(soong_config_variable("ril", "samsung_libril"), {
+        true: ["//hardware/samsung:libril_samsung_srcs"],
+        default: [
+            "ril.cpp",
+            "ril_event.cpp",
+            "ril_service.cpp",
+            "RilSapSocket.cpp",
+            "sap_service.cpp",
+        ],
+    }),
     shared_libs: [
         "android.hardware.radio@1.0",
         "android.hardware.radio@1.1",
@@ -49,7 +57,10 @@ cc_library_shared {
         "liblog",
         "librilutils",
         "libutils",
-    ],
+    ] + select(soong_config_variable("ril", "samsung_libril"), {
+        true: ["android.hardware.radio.deprecated@1.0"],
+        default: [],
+    }),
     static_libs: ["libprotobuf-c-nano-enable_malloc-32bit"],
     cflags: [
         "-Wall",
@@ -69,8 +80,25 @@ cc_library_shared {
             "-DOEM_HOOK_DISABLED",
         ],
         default: [],
+    }) + select(soong_config_variable("ril", "samsung_libril"), {
+        // SAMSUNG_NEXT_GEN_MODEM: what the make build sets for BOARD_MODEM_TYPE ss333 (Shannon).
+        // The Samsung sources were never built with -Werror.
+        true: [
+            "-DSAMSUNG_NEXT_GEN_MODEM",
+            "-Wno-error",
+        ],
+        default: [],
+    }),
+    // The Samsung directories come before the module directory (and before ril_headers), so
+    // that <ril_service.h>, <telephony/ril.h> and the other headers of the same names resolve
+    // to the Samsung ones.
+    include_dirs: ["external/nanopb-c"] + select(soong_config_variable("ril", "samsung_libril"), {
+        true: [
+            "hardware/samsung/ril/libril",
+            "hardware/samsung/ril/include",
+        ],
+        default: [],
     }),
-    include_dirs: ["external/nanopb-c"],
     header_libs: [
         "ril_headers",
     ],
